,"). The title of these psalms includes the Hebrew word for stairs, which some take to mean “ascending to Jerusalem.” These psalms (sometimes called the Songs of Ascents) take the reader on a pilgrimage to Jerusalem to praise God for his goodness to Israel throughout history."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.120.1-134.3","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":134,"endVerse":3,"startChapter":120,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.120.1-134.3","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[120,121,122,123,124,125,126,127,128,129,130,131,132,133,134],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"804bdc0d4264fc96adf7bf16357af3c33f1b33647dde7b70863e764ccb4e0941","sourceItemName":"Ps.120.1-134.3","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7297,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.120.1-134.3","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.120.1-134.3","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.132.1-18","r":"Ps.132.1-18","rawR":"Ps.132.1-18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.132.1-18","value":"Ps.132.1-18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 132"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," This psalm celebrates the Lord’s faithfulness to David. When David wanted to bring the Ark into Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.132.1-5","r":"Ps.132.1-5","rawR":"Ps.132.1-5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.132.1-5","value":"Ps.132.1-5"}],"t":"ref","v":"132:1-5"},"), the Lord granted the request and made Jerusalem his earthly home (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.132.6-10","r":"Ps.132.6-10","rawR":"Ps.132.6-10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.132.6-10","value":"Ps.132.6-10"}],"t":"ref","v":"132:6-10"},"). The choice of Jerusalem marked God’s election of David’s line (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.132.11-13","r":"Ps.132.11-13","rawR":"Ps.132.11-13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.132.11-13","value":"Ps.132.11-13"}],"t":"ref","v":"132:11-13"},"), of Zion (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.132.14-17","r":"Ps.132.14-17","rawR":"Ps.132.14-17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.132.14-17","value":"Ps.132.14-17"}],"t":"ref","v":"132:14-17"},"), and of the priesthood (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.132.9","r":"Ps.132.9","rawR":"Ps.132.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.132.9","value":"Ps.132.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"132:9"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.132.16","r":"Ps.132.16","rawR":"Ps.132.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.132.16","value":"Ps.132.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"16"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.132.1-18","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":132,"endVerse":18,"startChapter":132,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.132.1-18","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[132],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"19b873daffaf17b8b261408340a09c0957a96cc40d5418e15c1320c10707b087","sourceItemName":"Ps.132.1-18","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7349,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.132.1-18","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.132.1-18","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.132.6-10","r":"Ps.132.6-10","rawR":"Ps.132.6-10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.132.6-10","value":"Ps.132.6-10"}],"t":"ref","v":"132:6-10"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," These verses form a recollection of David’s moving the Ark of the Covenant to Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.6.1-15","r":"2Sam.6.1-15","rawR":"2Sam.6.1-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.6.1-15"